# The `Multiplicative ℤ`-action generated by an inner automorphism

This file supplies the twist `τ` used in the construction of the ambient ring
`P^{U_N}_{ω,τ}` of [JZLA20, Theorem 6.1] (see `PlanStep.md`).

If `D` is a subring of a ring `U`, `u : Uˣ` a unit normalising `D`, and
`e : ↥D ≃+* ↥D` the induced inner automorphism `x ↦ u x u⁻¹`
(`Subring.conjRingEquiv_exists`), then `D` carries an action of `Multiplicative ℤ` by
`(Multiplicative.ofAdd k) • x = e^k x` — the `k`-th power of the inner automorphism, i.e.
conjugation by `u^k`.

Everything here is `sorry`-free.
-/
import Mathlib

set_option autoImplicit false

set_option warn.classDefReducibility false

namespace Work.ORHughesFree

variable {U : Type*} [Ring U]

/-- **The `Multiplicative ℤ`-action on a ring generated by an automorphism.**  For
`e : R ≃+* R`, the group `Multiplicative ℤ` acts on `R` by `(Multiplicative.ofAdd k) • x = e^k x`.

This is the twist `τ` of `P^{U_N}_{ω,τ}` when `e` is the inner automorphism `x ↦ u x u⁻¹` of a
subring `D` normalised by a unit `u`. -/
noncomputable def RingEquiv.mulSemiringActionZpow {R : Type*} [Ring R] (e : R ≃+* R) :
    MulSemiringAction (Multiplicative ℤ) R where
  smul m x := (e ^ (Multiplicative.toAdd m)) x
  smul_zero m := map_zero _
  smul_add m x y := map_add _ _ _
  smul_one m := map_one _
  smul_mul m x y := map_mul _ _ _
  one_smul x := by
    show (e ^ (0 : ℤ)) x = x
    rw [zpow_zero]
    rfl
  mul_smul m n x := by
    show (e ^ (Multiplicative.toAdd (m * n))) x =
      (e ^ (Multiplicative.toAdd m)) ((e ^ (Multiplicative.toAdd n)) x)
    rw [show (Multiplicative.toAdd (m * n)) = Multiplicative.toAdd m + Multiplicative.toAdd n
      from rfl, zpow_add]
    rfl

/-- The action formula: `k • x = e^k x`. -/
theorem RingEquiv.mulSemiringActionZpow_smul {R : Type*} [Ring R] (e : R ≃+* R) (k : ℤ)
    (x : R) :
    letI := RingEquiv.mulSemiringActionZpow e
    (Multiplicative.ofAdd k • x : R) = (e ^ k) x := rfl

end Work.ORHughesFree
